reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["DraftKings Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $9.2B market cap on $6.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +39% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +22.4pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -5444% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $648M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 11 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 178.67\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -14.5% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 8.6% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit captu